\paragraph{Repo-level failure mode taxonomy.} Variant-level analysis ($n{=}48$, Appendix Table~\ref{tab:variant_level}) reveals three distinct failure modes (Table~\ref{tab:taxonomy}). The same formulation (\cls{}) fails in qualitatively different ways across models: Qwen3 at aggregation, DeepSeek at discrimination. \traj{} avoids aggregation penalty by predicting variant outcomes directly (75.35\% $\pm$ 5.00, DeepSeek-Coder, 6 seeds). No single formulation dominates; failure mode is a function of formulation $\times$ model $\times$ complexity.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\caption{Repo-level failure mode taxonomy. Variant-level majority baseline: 54.17\%.}
\label{tab:taxonomy}
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3pt}
\begin{tabular}{llcc}
\toprule
\textbf{Failure Mode} & \textbf{Representative} & \textbf{Fail Recall} & \textbf{Variant Acc} \\
\midrule
